<% content_for :title, "License badge — Printwright" %>
<div class="container" style="max-width: 720px">
  <h1>Embed your license badge</h1>
  <p>Every license gets an embeddable badge that links to its live on-chain check.
    Put it on your product page, your shop listing, anywhere — a buyer one click away
    from public proof beats a claim.</p>

  <p><%= render template: "verify/badge", formats: :svg,
           locals: { cert_id: "pw-4f2c8ab1d90e77", sandbox: false } %></p>

  <h2>Snippet</h2>
  <p class="t-small muted">Your verify link is on your receipt and your certificate; it ends in a
    random token that only you can hand out.</p>
  <pre class="mono t-small" style="overflow-x:auto"><code>&lt;a href="<%= verify_url("YOUR-VERIFY-TOKEN") %>"&gt;
  &lt;img src="<%= verify_badge_url("YOUR-VERIFY-TOKEN", format: :svg) %>"
       alt="Printwright licensed unit" width="200" height="36"&gt;
&lt;/a&gt;</code></pre>

  <h2>What it proves</h2>
  <p class="t-small">The badge itself proves nothing — the page it links to does: it reveals your
    certificate and recomputes the commitment anchored on the public Hedera mirror node. A printable
    certificate is available from the same page.</p>

  <h2>Independent verification widget</h2>
  <p class="t-small">For proof that does not depend on this marketplace, add the standalone widget to
    any HTML page. Give it the proof bundle from your delivery — as a URL, or pasted into the page —
    and it recomputes the commitment in the browser and compares it against the Hedera mirror.
    Pinning <code>topic-id</code> means a bundle anchored anywhere else cannot pass.</p>
  <pre class="mono t-small code-block"><code>&lt;script defer src="<%= request.base_url %>/printwright-verify-widget.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;printwright-verify bundle-url="<%= request.base_url %>/api/v1/certificates/YOUR-CERT-ID"
  topic-id="<%= ENV.fetch("HEDERA_HCS_TOPIC_ID", "0.0.9585069") %>" network="<%= Hedera::Network.name %>"&gt;
&lt;/printwright-verify&gt;</code></pre>
  <p class="t-small"><%= link_to "Open the plain HTML example", "/widget-example.html" %>.</p>
</div>
